# open62541-qnx change: interrupt-selfpipe
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# title: Fall back to a socket pair when pipe() is not available
# file: open62541.c
# upstream: arch/eventloop_posix_interrupt.c
# test: nopipe.server nopipe.client
#
# Without epoll the interrupt manager uses the self-pipe trick, and the
# default server configuration always contains an interrupt manager. On QNX
# pipe() is served by a separate process, the pipe manager. A target image
# that does not start it (many embedded images do not) makes pipe() fail, the
# interrupt manager does not start, and with it the event loop and the server.
#
# A local socket pair does the same job and needs only the network stack,
# which an OPC UA server needs in any case.
#
@@ hunk
